how to de-stress as an entrepreneur so i  got a great question for one of my  youtube viewers  love you guys marilyn who wrote in to  say hi evan can you make a video about  taking a day off or just turning it off  as an entrepreneur we're always working  both mind and body how do you destress  and detoxify yourself  from all these buildups do you turn off  your phone no emails  put up a do a disturb sign do you  believe in holistic cleansing  just wondering thank you thank you for  the great question  and running the business is not easy  right this isn't easy whoever said this  is going to be a walk in the park  they're kidding themselves this is this  is the hardest thing you're ever going  to do in your life  if you're pouring your heart into it and  you're facing rejection you're not  seeing the momentum  this is hard and you are gonna get  stressed out and  and just battling through and staying  motivated helps but i'm gonna give you  my three  suggestions to help you de-stress  maybe detoxify but help you build a  better business one that you're proud of  and one that you can continue on running  number one is eliminate distractions you  mentioned do i turn off my email do i  turn off my phone  i don't have a phone i don't use a cell  phone number  i don't check my email during the day i  don't check my  social media accounts you know i have  designated times for everything  it's really important if you want to  stay as stress-free as possible as an  entrepreneur  to have dedicated times of focused work  i prefer 90 minute chunks and i say in  this 90 minutes i'm going to focus on  this and only this  and every time you get distracted you  lose your focus and then to get back  into where you were  was it's hard right you lose your  momentum and it stresses you out because  you want to get this thing done  it's like you keep getting interrupted  and you can't make any progress  i remember last night i got an idea i  wanted to i wanted to interview howard  schultz who's the founder of  starbucks as the chairman of starbucks  from my book  and uh so i started writing him an email  i started writing  and and my wife nina uh  says hey evan can you come look at the  freezer and like ah you know let me  finish  let me finish uh writing this note  and and i'll be right there and then i'm  still writing i'm so right and she  thought i'd finish i said hey can you  come look at the freezer i'm like oh  fine fine i'll come look at the freezer  and there's these icicles that were  forming or whatever  and then i got frustrated and then i  went back and i looked at my email like  i totally forgot what i was doing  and i had to get back in the zone and  like i just wanted to finish  and so that happens to a lot of people  all the time you keep getting  interrupted with people knocking at your  door or calling or emailing you  and that you're always in reactive mode  instead of  chunking out times blocking it off and  saying this is what i'm going to work on  for this 90 minutes so that's what i do  90-minute chunks 15-minute breaks in  between to let your brain  you know de-stress a little bit and  shift gears and just not look at the  computer or whatever you're doing  and then into your next 90-minute chunk  and don't let people  walk all over your time you've got to  set up limits and say  this is what i'm doing nobody bugged me  and and  you know i don't check my phone or email  any of that stuff so you got to turn all  that stuff off  number two is design a better business  design a better  business i hate the idea of  i'm gonna work so hard on my business  and and stress myself out so much and  then just  take a break from it all and build up  the  the the fortitude to go off and do it  all again  and invest all this time and then have  to go take another vacation i think your  business  you are you're not working with somebody  else right this is your business you  could design  whatever you want to do you get to  create the world that you want to create  so design a world that supports you i  don't think you have to be all stressed  out  and then take a break from it all your  business should be designed  in a way that you get energy from it it  shouldn't be an energy stealer  the things that you do in your company  should lift you up  and not super stress you out all the  time i make these videos  not because somebody told me to do  videos not because it's a smart  business thing to do but i love it like  i love being able to answer questions i  love being able to reach people  your comments mean the world to me they  make my morning every day  when i'm eating my lentils and checking  out my computer that's the first thing i  look at because  it gives me energy you guys fueled me to  do more and to be better  and if there was something that kept  stealing my energy kept stressing me out  i would eliminate it  gone like that it does not need to be in  my life  and i'll focus on something else that  gives me energy so design your business  in a way that supports you and feeds you  instead of drains you  and number three is follow your flow  as much as i have my day scheduled and i  have my 90 minute chunks at a time  and you know wednesday is my video day  so i'm sitting here recording  all of these videos i like to stay in  flow  as much as possible try to get the flow  and listen to your body and having  an awareness over what you're feeling  right now  and how it's translated into your work  and so what i mean by that is sometimes  you're working on something and you're  feeling it and you're in the flow and  just um awesome stuff is being cranked  out  and you know that you're creating great  work and then other times it feels like  a struggle  you know like ah like you can't get in  the zone and the  quality you know is suffering to force  that  doesn't work like you know you're not  going to get great results from it so  stop and go do something else so when  i'm making these videos  you know i do two videos every day so  like 14 videos a week  are coming out and i got to sit down and  record these things and answer your  questions and do all this stuff  and some wednesdays i sit down and and i  can pump out 20 videos and it's like  boom i'm on fire  answering questions you know i had a  great session with jenny before i'm  drinking my smoothies whatever it is and  and i am just killing it and other  wednesdays i feel like i'm not in my  rhythm yet and i'm  you know just not hitting it and so i'll  stop  early maybe i'll do five videos or maybe  i get to  my tenth video and and i've poured  everything into it it's like you know  what  that's it i have no more left there is  nothing left here  to create another video i feel like my  next one won't be good so i'm going to  stop  and so it's designing the business back  to number two designing the business  where i don't need to have  14 videos every single week i can create  more one week and less the next week  and so on so i've designed it to support  me and i can stay in my flow  so remember if you want to de-stress as  an entrepreneur number one eliminate  distractions number two  design a better business and number  three follow your flow  believe for those who watching if you  liked the video you want to see more  just like it you can click on the  subscribe button to subscribe to the  channel  thank you so much for watching and i'll  see you soon  you
 

